To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas, you can follow these steps:

1. Define your Mongoose schema for each nested object. For example:

```typescript
import { Prop, SchemaFactory } from '@nestjs/mongoose';
import { Type } from 'class-transformer';
import { IsOptional, MaxLength } from 'class-validator';

export interface IAddress {
  street: string;
  city: string;
  state: string;
  zip: number;
}

@SchemaFactory.createForClass(Address)
@Schema({ _id: false })
export class AddressSchema {
  @Prop()
  @MaxLength(255)
  street: string;

  @Prop()
  @MaxLength(255)
  city: string;

  @Prop()
  @MaxLength(255)
  state: string;

  @Prop()
  @Type(() => Number)
  zip: number;
}

export interface IPerson {
  name: string;
  age: number;
  address?: IAddress;
}

@SchemaFactory.createForClass(Person)
@Schema()
export class PersonSchema {
  @Prop()
  name: string;

  @Prop()
  age: number;

  @Prop({ type: AddressSchema })
  @IsOptional()
  address: IAddress;
}
```

In the above example, we have created two interfaces `IAddress` and `IPerson`, and their corresponding Mongoose schemas `AddressSchema` and `PersonSchema`. Here, `address` is an optional field in `IPerson`.

