The implementation follows the dot notation pattern, splitting the path into an array of keys, then iterating over them to access the corresponding values. If any key is missing, the function returns an empty array immediately. Finally, the last key is accessed using square brackets notation instead of dot notation, since this syntax is required when the key is not a simple identifier but contains special characters like numbers or dots.

